Completed with local and canonical CI proof.

Red reproduction: after pnpm platform:check passed, a PATH shadow containing a GNU-timeout stub caused the old verify:db entrypoint to fail before database checks with the stock-macOS missing-timeout message.

Implementation: replaced GNU timeout with scripts/run-with-deadline.mjs; the whole verify:db chain runs inside one bounded shell, stdout/stderr and child status are forwarded, POSIX process groups receive TERM then KILL after grace, and timeout exits 124. Added deterministic success/failure/timeout/process-child tests and updated the repository-policy regression.

Proof:
- focused runner tests: 5/5 passed;
- combined runner + repository-policy tests: 20/20 passed;
- rtk proxy pnpm typecheck: all 6 packages passed;
- exact Fallow committed range 23487afdf0ee672ce920b41a73e2cf3a57c65106..f2a59afed96025f64d96707ffb6d62551b403fe6: passed, no findings;
- rtk git diff --check: passed;
- exact GitHub Actions run 29260906835 for f2a59afed96025f64d96707ffb6d62551b403fe6: all 3 jobs passed;
- GLM advisory attempted for this exact range, but Z.ai returned HTTP 400 and produced no review.

Proves: the canonical DB command no longer depends on GNU timeout and the deadline wrapper has tested bounded process behavior on the current Linux environment; the committed CI gate is green.

Does not prove: a real macOS runner or stock Apple shell/container execution, Windows support, production deployment, or direct observed TERM-handler output (the implementation sends TERM then KILL and process-group termination is tested, but handler output is timing-sensitive and not asserted). The local Node is v26, while the canonical repository contract is Node 22; CI is the canonical Node 22 proof.

Rollback: revert the runner, package script, and focused tests; restore the previous platform-policy contract only if macOS support is explicitly withdrawn.

