- exact code commit 1e6f870790e7127523d29e0ae13df69f47e08add passed Ubuntu Typecheck/tests/eval and Ubuntu DB in run 29262370547; its macOS job failed before the later provider bootstrap fixes.
- current rerun 29262585641 again passed macOS; Ubuntu DB returned the intended bounded timeout 124, so this is recorded as a separate CI runtime follow-up rather than hidden.

Proves: a real GitHub macOS-14 Node22 environment reaches and passes both canonical fast and DB profiles, including disposable Postgres/pgvector and bounded process behavior.

Does not prove: Ubuntu DB completion under the current 120-second deadline in every run; PostgreSQL 16 parity on macOS (Homebrew provider is PostgreSQL 17); every local filesystem/container setup; Windows; production deployment; or product READY.

Residual follow-up: investigate why the canonical Ubuntu DB profile now repeatedly reaches the explicit 124 deadline. This is not a macOS portability failure and is not evidence that the KRN product is READY.

